    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "THE ONE RULE, and it is already written twice in this repository",
      "prov:value": "The repository and knowledge-graph scales share ONE verdict function,\n`schemas/kg/layer-direction.ts` (bean `j79e`). An edge is **wrong-direction**\nexactly when its target layer is not among what the source layer declares it\nmay reach — `ALLOWED` for repos, `needs` plus itself for instances — and no\nreasoned permit names it. An instance with no `needs` is **undetermined**,\nreported in its own column, never read as clean. The function stops at\ndirection: whether an allowed edge is a *restatement* or *essential* is the\nadjudicator's call, so those edges stay `unclassified` with the verdict as\ntheir basis.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean j79e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "THE ONE RULE, and it is already written twice in this repository",
      "prov:value": "**The direction count is the one detangle number that is GRADED**, and it is\ngraded in a gate of its own — `bun run cat kg:detangle:direction`, blocking in CI\nsince the owner's Option 2 ruling on bean `p11x` (2026-09-30). Everything else\nthis tool measures stays **pinned**: `kg:detangle:check` fails on a stale or\norphaned sidecar and never on a number, because the carve is an adjudication a\nperson makes and grading it would be the tool overruling the adjudicator.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean p11x",
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "THE ONE RULE, and it is already written twice in this repository",
      "prov:value": "- **`undetermined` edges** — an endpoint's instance declares no `needs`. Failing\n  on these would be the gate deciding a layering nobody declared.\n- **the denominator** — the count is over the edges that **resolve**. Dangling\n  refs (bean `blv9`) are excluded before any edge is classified, so a `0` is\n  *\"0 among the edges that resolve\"*, which is the weaker claim. The gate prints\n  the excluded count and its breakdown, because a blocking gate that hides its\n  denominator can pass because an edge failed to resolve rather than because the\n  layering held. Bean `cjvs` owns triaging them.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean blv9",
        "bean cjvs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "THE ONE RULE, and it is already written twice in this repository",
      "prov:value": "**It is not `check:partition`'s second opinion.** That tool's root is one\ninstance, so it partitions a **future** layout by path rule among that\ninstance's own modules; this checks the **present** layout against declared\n`needs` across instances. `bf5l` measured them disagreeing — a real\n`cat-harness → folio-assistant-core` import gave `check:partition` `0` and this\n`1`. Either can be green while the other is red, and Phase I.1 of the migration\nplan now needs both."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "THE ONE RULE, and it is already written twice in this repository",
      "prov:value": "**At term scale** — a glossary declared `ordered` (owner, 2026-09-29, of\nbootstrap's terms: *\"logically tight, non self-referential\"*). Each term's\n`requires` must point UP, and `checkDeclaredOrder` in\n`schemas/kg/dependency-order.ts` names every forward, self and missing use. It is\nthe block-scale rule with terms for blocks: a forward `requires` is a forward\nedge, and two terms defined by each other are a cycle **no ordering removes**,\nso the moves are the same three — drop the use, merge the two terms, or factor\nthe shared idea into a term above both. The rule and its form on the page are\nin `glossary-terms` §\"Ordered glossaries\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. Declare in place",
      "prov:value": "The worked example was a `methodologies/` graph in the WHO base harness,\ndeclared at repository scope in `cat-harness/cat-harness.json` while it still\nsat in this tree, so that the directory lifted out whole when that harness\nbecame its own repository (2026-10) — which is the claim, demonstrated. (The example was `smart-kg/methodologies/grade.md` until\n2026-09-24, when GRADE became a skill plus code lists — bean `wg7r`.)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean wg7r",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Measurement",
      "prov:value": "> The same false comfort at a different join, and it has its own skill —\n> `covered-is-not-reachable`: *\"A skill showing as covered is not evidence that\n> its code is reachable.\"* Coverage is a relation between a Tool and a **skill**,\n> never between a Tool and a command, so `check:tools` answers green over\n> mechanisms nothing can reach. Found three times in one session, and measured\n> by hand at **229 of 868 code files reachable from no node, collapsing to 13\n> groups** — which is a partition measurement in everything but name. Read that\n> skill before concluding a corpus is covered; it is not restated here."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Measurement",
      "prov:value": "**2. The count rises when the measurement improves, and that is correct.**\nWrong-direction edges went **43 → 49** when thirteen previously-unjudged edges\nwere folded in. The commit that did it is titled *\"judge the last six modules —\nand the count goes UP, correctly\"*. **A detangling count that only ever falls\nis a count that is not being measured honestly.**"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Judgement",
      "prov:value": "**10. The triage question, in either of two equivalent forms.** *\"Does it act\non the PLATFORM or on CONTENT?\"* and *\"does it need a folio to have anything to\ndo?\"* Four independent sessions converged on these two phrasings. The owner's\nsharper cut: *\"needed to RUN a process is tooling; DESCRIBES one is core.\"*\nAnd the one-line test for the renderable side: *\"if it renders, it is not the\nharness's.\"*"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Judgement",
      "prov:value": "**14. The fix is not an exemption, it is the right owner.** An exemption is\nwhat you write when ownership is genuinely ambiguous, and then it carries its\nreason inline — one entry records *\"omitting it cost 3 wrong-direction edges\nthe day #468 merged\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#468"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Enforcement",
      "prov:value": "**16. Watch the new gate FAIL before trusting it.** Every enforcement step in\nthis corpus records a deliberate re-introduction producing exit 1. A gate that\ncannot fail is indistinguishable from one that passed — bean `xom7`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xom7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declare a falsifier, and mean it",
      "prov:value": "**It fired.** Classifying nineteen scripts alone took edges 5 → 12, the seven\nnew edges were read rather than argued away, and the order of operations\nchanged because of it. A falsifier that never fires is decoration; this one\nrewrote the plan."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declare a falsifier, and mean it",
      "prov:value": "## The failure this practice exists to prevent, and it is mine"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "The failure this practice exists to prevent, and it is mine",
      "prov:value": "> \"I reported in PR #469 that classifying `src/types.ts` as core *'was tried\n> and measured, and the edge is unchanged'*. The experiment was\n> **INCONCLUSIVE**: the harness `exact` list is consulted first, so the core\n> entry never applied. **I noticed at the time, said so, and then reported the\n> conclusion as measured anyway.** The conclusion stands; the evidence I gave\n> for it was not the evidence I had.\"",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#469"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/graph-detanglement.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Related",
      "prov:value": "- [`graph-rendering`](graph-rendering.md) — drawing the graph being\n  partitioned, with each group's detangle numbers beside it. The UML overview\n  pages show them per sub-graph.\n- `placement.md` — the sibling SOP, for where a NEW node goes. Same shape:\n  numbered steps, a stop, a closing checklist.\n- `covered-is-not-reachable` — the reachability half, and the rule that\n  \"reachability is PLURAL\": the question is not which caller a mechanism should\n  have but what should be able to START it. Pointed at rather than absorbed,\n  per `AGENTS.md`'s warning against minting something to take over what an\n  existing object already owns.\n- `docs/architecture/migration-plan.md` — the phased plan for this\n  repository's own five-repo cut, including the Phase II per-repo gate.\n- `scripts/repo-partition.ts` — the instrument. Its comment prose is where much\n  of the above was recorded first.\n- `schemas/kg/layer-direction.ts` — the one wrong-direction verdict both\n  `check:partition` and `kg:detangle` call."
    }
  ]
